{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794984549,"nonce":"A9PubMtQv0fmr5RO9MBPCNSOFM8=","title":"Plan an opt-in content-addressable asset catalog and KyuGraph projection in the hxn-assets monorepo, layered over hxn-file. hxnme consumes these APIs later. The user owns KyuGraph; the local source is /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/kyugraph.","message":"Proposed Haxe metadata on asset declarations: @:asset(\"address\", \"relative/path\"), independently opted-in @:contentAddressed(\"sha256\"), and @:projectAsset(\"schema-name\"). World/entity declarations opt in separately with @:projectEntity(\"schema-name\"); concrete metadata names are provisional until the compile-time API is implemented. Normal asset loading, saves and preferences do not require hashing, graph storage, a server or a KyuGraph runtime.\n\nSeparate identities: logical asset address (stable alias), immutable content ID (algorithm-qualified digest of exact stored bytes), and entity/world-instance ID (including world and instance namespace). A changed asset updates the address-to-content edge; moving an entity does not change the content identity. Hash cooked payload bytes, retain source-to-variant provenance, verify expected digests on load and reject mismatches before caching or projection.\n\nProjection schema: AssetAddress -\u003e RESOLVES_TO -\u003e AssetContent; AssetContent -\u003e DEPENDS_ON -\u003e AssetContent; EntityInstance -\u003e USES_ASSET -\u003e AssetContent; World -\u003e CONTAINS -\u003e EntityInstance; entity PARENT_OF/ATTACHED_TO and typed application relationships. Store local/world transforms, coordinate-space/world identifiers, bounds, units and frame/revision on instances rather than asset blobs. Keep authoritative game/scene state in the application; graph data is a rebuildable, versioned query projection.\n\nLocal KyuGraph evidence: crates/kyu-graph re-exports the public API; Connection::query_with_params binds typed values; Connection::apply_delta accepts DeltaBatchBuilder and atomically commits a batch with idempotent upserts. Use parameter bindings and stable batch/source IDs instead of composing Cypher values into strings. Schema migrations, removal/tombstones and reconnect/replay must be idempotent; bound/coalesce updates, never block rendering or run one transaction per transform per frame.\n\nQueries must combine asset identity/dependencies with world membership, entity relationships, instances using a content ID, and region/bounds predicates. The inspected KyuGraph code does not establish a dedicated spatial index/query API; validate that capability before claiming efficient geometric queries. Begin with explicit numeric positions/AABBs and a coarse world-space cell relation if supported, then measure/index appropriately. A canvas/world ID and transform revision prevent mixing coordinates from different worlds or stale parent transforms.\n\nPlatform boundaries: the inspected KyuGraph kyu-api currently brings JIT, Arrow Flight/Tokio and storage dependencies. Do not silently embed it in browser/iOS packages or assume its portability. Plan a separate optional adapter and a backend-neutral projection batch/query interface: supported native embedded use, and an application-configured connected endpoint for mobile/browser when embedded support is unavailable. Network/auth/authority policy belongs to the connected application. Project only opted-in fields, not saves, preferences or arbitrary file contents.\n\nValidation: annotation absent produces no hash/projection work or graph dependency; deterministic IDs across runtimes; duplicate content deduplication while two scene instances retain distinct transforms; cooked variants/provenance; address rebinding and deletion; graph replay/rebuild; moved/parented entities and world changes; query relationships plus bounds; stale/reordered revisions; bounded queue/reconnect; native/mobile/browser adapter contract coverage. Record platform limitations explicitly.\n\nParent file-access issue: 49624d318b0b2d8efec7e26ccd271c6004e5150e4fe8b5dd33e105ee21c472fb. Parent hxnme plan: 88ad5eff5f418581d790175f13ad89d85d24c50e980dca23033b4d884329b3cd. This projection planning does not replace the M0 bundled-file and persistent-save round-trip requirement.","files":null}]}